# The clipboard's images (#300 finished, docs/clipboard-plan.md "Generation 2") on the agents' Duo (iOS 27.1):
# the Share Clipboard group with Include Images off (the default), on, and for a Mac that shares text alone
# (no row), sideways and upright; the chip's place with the new notes. Against main's: the group gains its row
# and words, the rest of the panel is as it was.
#   Scripts/harness-photos.sh Scripts/harness-photos/clipboard-images-duo.cases --baseline origin/main
duo-clip-images-off        -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillSettings 1 -SillSettingsScroll clipboard --pose=flat-landscape --wait=5
duo-clip-images-on         -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillSettings 1 -SillSettingsScroll clipboard -Sill.clipboardImages 1 --pose=flat-landscape --wait=5
duo-clip-older-mac         -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillSettings 1 -SillSettingsScroll clipboard -SillMockClipboard 1 --pose=flat-landscape --wait=5
duo-clip-upright-on        -SillLayout 669x951 -SillHinge flat -SillSettings 1 -SillSettingsScroll clipboard -Sill.clipboardImages 1 --wait=5
duo-clip-note-sending      -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillClipboardNote sending --pose=flat-landscape
duo-clip-note-unreadable   -SillLayout 951x669 -SillHinge flat -SillClipboardNote unreadable --pose=flat-landscape
